ClearPDF NOTICE

This project depends on PdfBox-Android by Tom Roush, used for lossless PDF page
operations (merge, split, organize) and text extraction.
Source: https://github.com/TomRoush/PdfBox-Android
PdfBox-Android is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and is itself a
port of Apache PDFBox (https://pdfbox.apache.org/).

This project uses Google ML Kit (document scanner and on-device text recognition)
for the scanning and text-selection features only.

The image editor adapts source code from ImageToolbox by T8RIN (Malik Mukhametzyanov),
Copyright (c) 2026, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
Source: https://github.com/T8RIN/ImageToolbox
Adapted code keeps the original Apache-2.0 header plus a "Modified by ClearPDF" line:
the free-corners perspective warp (lib/opencv-tools, with OpenCV replaced by
android.graphics.Matrix) and draw-engine geometry/paint/flood-fill code (feature/draw).
The image editor also depends on GPUImage for Android by CyberAgent (Apache-2.0).

